      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T14:08:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure we actually need a new capability for this specific thing. Essentially, if we are accepting module-scope variables with `in`/`out` address spaces, then `blend_src` on those things will always be allowed.\n\nRight now we just always accept in/out module-scope variables AFAICT (the fuzzer will never produce them because they are not in the protobuf). Maybe we should have a capability for that whole mode of shader IO instead of creating more fine-grained checks?",
      "revId": "fba2fd1d6d96b12ac20e5b2f41d8ff8691958d60",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4f1c749_b96b5009",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/validator.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3106,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T15:08:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am fine with it being a wider scope capability, i.e. `kAllowShaderIOExceptions`, since we don\u0027t want to end up with a bunch of capabilities that are enabled/disabled in the same situation.\n\nI am just unsure of what existing capability this should be associated/renamed for this purpose. The only one I can see that is obviously about MSV + I/O,  `kAllowUnannotatedModuleIOVariables`, is actually doing the opposite, allowings MSVs without `in`/`out`.",
      "parentUuid": "2df7e50f_9a02ce37",
      "revId": "fba2fd1d6d96b12ac20e5b2f41d8ff8691958d60",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79150b4b_679ce5e0",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/validator.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3106,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T20:58:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s no existing capability for `in`/`out`, we just always accept them. So we can either create a new capability for shader IO in module-scope variables which guards the use of `in`/`out`, or we just leave things as they are where they are just always allowed, and therefore blend_src on a MSV is also always allowed.\n\nThe former is probably better, although it is beyond the scope of this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "d4f1c749_b96b5009",
      "revId": "fba2fd1d6d96b12ac20e5b2f41d8ff8691958d60",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e8750ea_362e413d",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/validator.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3106,
      "author": {
